-- Each states what the citing words need: that the target is what the citing words say it is (four assertions), that a chapter named by a letter and a digit stands in the consolidation under that name (one assertion),
-- and that the Hebrew date and the Gregorian date given for one day name the same day (one assertion).
-- The texts quoted in il46-cross-references.l4 say otherwise for each. Nothing here is edited to make it pass.

